1
00:00:02,472 --> 00:00:04,136
(Q11&12（多选）) Good morning.

2
00:00:04,136 --> 00:00:13,200
My name's Lucy Crittenden, and l'm the Director of Operations for an organisation that arranges volunteering in this part of the country.

3
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:19,351
I'm hoping I can persuade one or two of you to become volunteers yourselves.

4
00:00:19,351 --> 00:00:24,472
Let me start by briefly explaining what we mean by volunteering.

5
00:00:24,472 --> 00:00:32,764
Volunteers are teenagers and adults who choose to spend some time, unpaid, helping other people in some way.

6
00:00:32,764 --> 00:00:39,245
Most volunteers devote two or three hours to this every week, while a few do much more.

7
00:00:39,245 --> 00:00:45,378
The people they help may have physical or behavioural difficulties, for example.

8
00:00:45,378 --> 00:00:52,273
Volunteers can do all sorts of things, depending on their own abilities and interests.

9
00:00:52,273 --> 00:01:05,477
[A：干扰项A，只是教你cook , 不是deliver meals（送外卖）] If they're supporting a family that's struggling, for example, they may be able to give them tips on cooking, or recommend how to plan their budget or how to shop sensibly on their income.

10
00:01:05,477 --> 00:01:13,886
(Q11&12-A) [Q11&12答案句- A：decorating] They might even do some painting or wallpapering, perhaps alongside any members of the family who are able to do it.

11
00:01:13,886 --> 00:01:18,988
(Q11&12-E) [Q11&12答案句-E:babysitting] Or even do some babysitting so that parents can go out for a while.

12
00:01:18,988 --> 00:01:24,156
(Q13&14（多选）) The benefit from volunteering isn't only for the people being helped.

13
00:01:24,156 --> 00:01:44,569
(Q13&14-E) [Q13&14答案句E： boost their employment prospects. be valuable on CV 求职简历] Volunteers also gain from it: they're using their skills to cope with somebody's mental or physical ill health, and volunteering may be a valuable element of their CV when they're applying for jobs: employers usually look favourably on someone who's given up time to help others.

14
00:01:44,569 --> 00:01:51,620
(Q13&14-B) [Q13&14答案句- B： having  a sense of purpose] Significantly, most volunteers feel that what they're doing gives them a purpose in their lives.

15
00:01:51,620 --> 00:01:59,579
[Q1314干扰项C，仅是speaker自己的观点，别人don't have the feeling 排除方式：否定] And in my opinion, they're lucky in that respect, as many people don't have that feeling.

16
00:01:59,579 --> 00:02:09,733
(Q15（Matching）) Now I'd like to tell you what some of our volunteers have said about what they do, to give you an idea of the range of ways in which they can help people.

17
00:02:09,733 --> 00:02:15,440
Habib supports an elderly lady who's beginning to show signs of dementia.&nbsp;

18
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:25,952
Once a week they, along with other elderly people, go to the local community centre, where a group of people come in and sing.

19
00:02:25,952 --> 00:02:34,960
[Q15答案句F： youth=past times] The songs take the listeners back to their youth, and for a little while they can forget the difficulties that they face now.

20
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:38,933
(Q16) Our volunteer Consuela is an amazing woman.

21
00:02:38,933 --> 00:02:44,374
She has difficulty walking herself, but she doesn't let that stop her.

22
00:02:44,374 --> 00:02:51,586
She helps a couple of people with similar difficulties, who had almost stopped walking altogether.

23
00:02:51,586 --> 00:02:59,971
[Q16答案句A：overcoming physical difficulties 全都是在说这个含义] By using herself as an example, Consuela encourages them to walk more and more.&nbsp;

24
00:02:59,971 --> 00:03:10,370
(Q17) Minh visits a young man who lives alone and can't leave his home on his own, so he hardly ever saw anyone.&nbsp;

25
00:03:10,370 --> 00:03:18,987
[Q17答案句E：escape isolation] But together they go out to the cinema, or to see friends the young man hadn't been able to visit for a long time.

26
00:03:18,987 --> 00:03:22,812
(Q18) Tanya visits an elderly woman once a week.&nbsp;

27
00:03:22,812 --> 00:03:30,763
[Q18答案句G： start a new hobby = get interested ,后面很长篇幅都在说这个] When the woman found out that Tanya is a professional dressmaker, she got interested.

28
00:03:30,763 --> 00:03:38,425
Tanya showed her some soft toys she'd made, and the woman decided to try it herself.

29
00:03:38,425 --> 00:03:45,366
And now she really enjoys it, and spends hours making toys.

30
00:03:45,366 --> 00:03:53,028
They're not perhaps up to Tanya's standard yet, but she gains a lot of pleasure from doing it.

31
00:03:53,028 --> 00:03:59,371
(Q19) Alexei is a volunteer with a family that faces a number of difficulties.&nbsp;

32
00:03:59,371 --> 00:04:12,776
[Q19答案句D：solve problems independently = do sth themselves] By calmly talking over possible solutions with family members, he's helping them to realise that they aren't helpless, and that they can do something themselves to improve their situation.

33
00:04:12,776 --> 00:04:17,060
This has been great for their self-esteem.

34
00:04:17,060 --> 00:04:23,143
(Q20) And the last volunteer I'll mention, though there are plenty more, is Juba.

35
00:04:23,143 --> 00:04:32,082
[Q20答案句C：improve their communication skills = not good at talking,反义对应] She volunteers with a teenage girl with learning difficulties, who wasn't very good at talking to other people.

36
00:04:32,082 --> 00:04:42,325
Juba's worked very patiently with her, and now the girl is far better at expressing herself, and understanding other people. Juba

37
00:04:42,325 --> 00:04:47,804
OK, I hope that's given you an idea of what volunteering is all about.

38
00:04:47,804 --> 00:04:50,304
Now I'd like ...

